// Name :
"P27484507" "Praetor Duncan"
// ProfessionString :
"P2568636875" "Praetor"
// DescriptionString :
"P2079165079" "Being the daughter of a famous and universally loved super heroine never sat well with Praetor Duncan. She rebelled from a very early age and when she hit puberty and her powers kicked in she decided enough was enough. After killing her mother, the infamous Miss Liberty, she started making a name for herself. She is now a respected Praetor, although there are some who believe she does not deserve such a high title."
// InteractionRequiresText :
// LocationString :
// HelloString :
"P2955958899" "I thought Praetoria had a lot of problems. People on Primal Earth seem to know how to <i>really</i> screw things up."
// IDontKnowYouString :
// NoTasksRemainingString :
"P1917975977" "<color orange>You're unable to get in touch with Praetor Duncan.</color>"
// PlayerBusyString :
"P914596440" "{HeroName}, a girl <i>really</i> hates it when someone tries to ask them for something when they're already way too busy with other things."
// FailsafeLevelString :
// IntroString :
// IntroAcceptString :
// IntroduceOneContact :
"P3448102945" "<color orange>You'll have to now travel back in time and find Sister Solaris in order to combat Mot.</color>"
// IntroduceTwoContacts :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - PraetorDuncan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Everything Text :
"P2967232007" "Well well, if it isn't {HeroName}. You can imagine that I wasn't surprised when I heard you were here in Dark Astoria. You and I have quite the history together, don't we? Mm, there was that time at the bottom of Cole's tower... you gave me quite the 'thrashing', didn't you?<br><br>Oh, and you had also found out that nasty little business with the Destroyers. It was quite sad that my time with them was gone, I was having <i>such</i> a great time.<br><br>You really do know how to ruin a girl's fun, don't you? But, that's neither here nor there. Today, you and I are talking in order to deal with this little problem that the Primal people have, which is Diabolique."
// Answer Text :
"P1028250016" "You must be out of your mind if you think I'll work with you, Duncan."
// Answer Text :
"P3906070191" "I should've known she'd resurface after recovering her talisman."
// Answer Text :
"P314648574" "Let's just skip the bantering, Duncan. What do you know about Diabolique?"
// Page OutOfYourMind Text :
"P2265545996" "Do you think I'm Tilman, {HeroName}. Now, <i>she</i> is someone who is, or rather <i>was</i>, out of her mind, don't you agree?<br><br>No, I'm just manipulative and diabolical, but in this case, I'm willing to put that aside for that greater good nonsense. 'Emperor' Cole has ordered me to come down here with an Olympian and track down Diabolique. Of course, he said it's because of White's failure to keep Diabolique's amulet safe. Haha!<br><br>The whole thing doesn't really matter, anyway. Praetoria's days are numbered. Battle Maiden's gone, no one knows what happened to Neuron and Bobcat, Siege and Nightstar are old news, Marauder's gone into self-exile, Anti-Matter wandered off, and Praetor Tilman's dead. There's not a lot of us left, but stupid Cole still thinks it's his responsibility to save this world from Diabolique. Can you believe it?"
// Answer Text :
"P3408404193" "And he sent you of all people to handle this?"
// Page HandleThis Text :
"P474592577" "Well, {HeroName}, I actually volunteered to help. I would <i>so</i> hate to see Primal Earth wiped off the face of the universe. After all, it has one of the entrances to the Pocket D, and that place is just a <i>blast</i>!<br><br>It was between myself of Chimera, and to be honest, that guy has his hands <i>really</i> full, what with trying to salvage what's left of Praetoria with Cole."
// Answer Text :
"P3353482116" "Well, what do you know about Diabolique?"
// Page TalismanKnown Text :
"P3445301931" "Yes, well, I didn't imagine she'd skip off to Primal Earth after getting her talisman back. I was <i>really</i> hoping she'd continue making a scene in First Ward; that way, I could've seen Cole rip her little ghostly head off her flimsy ghostly body and watched her ectoplasm <i>ooze</i> out.<br><br>I guess she was smarter than I took her for, running away to Primal Earth. Though, if she <i>was</i> smart, she would've gone to a place where Cole wasn't currently invading."
// Answer Text :
"P3396500786" "What do you know about Diabolique's presence here?"
// Page FirstWard Text :
"P1300464616" "Well well, if it isn't {HeroName}. You can imagine that I wasn't surprised when I saw you were here in Dark Astoria. You and I have quite the history together, don't we? Mm, there was that time at the bottom of Cole's tower... you gave me quite the 'thrashing', didn't you?<br><br>But, that's neither here nor there. Today, you and I are talking in order to deal with this little problem that these Primal people have, which is Diabolique."
// Page Fixadine Text :
"P991738725" "Well well, if it isn't {HeroName}. You can imagine that I wasn't surprised when I saw you were here in Dark Astoria. You and I have quite the history together, don't we?  Like the time you found out that nasty little business with the Destroyers. That was quite sad that my fun with them was gone, I was having <i>such</i> a great time.<br><br>You really do know how to ruin a girl's fun, don't you? But, that's neither here nor there. Today, you and I are talking in order to deal with this little problem that these Primal people have, which is Diabolique."
// Page Regular Text :
"P4208345380" "Well well, if it isn't {HeroName}. You can imagine that I wasn't surprised when I heard you were here in Dark Astoria. After all, you're the talk of the Primal Earth town, aren't you? {Hero.gender=male Mr|Mrs} big bad Incarnate, {Hero.type=hero acting like the savior of the world with your new powers.|making the world terrified of a big bad villain having such naughty powers.} Today, you and I are talking in order to deal with this little problem that these Primal people have, which is Diabolique.<br><br>In case you're unaware, I don't know <i>how</i> you wouldn't know, I am <color yellow>Praetor Duncan</color>, of Praetoria. Now, let's get down to business, shall we?"
// Answer Text :
"P1873639492" "What do you know about Diabolique?"
// Page KnowAboutDiabolique Text :
"P3235334610" "Diabolique is an evil ghost that doesn't belong in the world of the living. After she gained her freedom in First Ward, she must've fled our dimension to come to this one.<br><br>My guess is that she wasn't too sure what she was looking for when she arrived, but she sensed the power of this Mot growing stronger. Diabolique is somehow working together with Mot now... that part I have <i>no</i> idea about. I <i>do</i> know that her presence here is responsible for the <color red>Talons of Vengeance</color> showing up. They've been tracking her down for who knows how long.<br><br>From what myself and the Olympian have looked into, it seems that the Talons recruited the Knives to purge this world of so-called 'injustice'. I guess those harpies had their eye off of Primal Earth for far too long and realized there was a lot of work to do!"
// Answer Text :
"P4094784178" "Do you know where to find Diabolique?"
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 


